==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Le'Behemoth]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*10 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Zollow]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Zollow]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 3.33~5 seconds<sup>100f~150f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Zollow]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The combination of Aku support with strong Zombie attackers can pose a large threat without a strategy. You'll spend most of the time wearing down Le'Behemoth while sending cheap and quick counters for the Zombies. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]'s quick foreswing, cheap cost, and speedy recharge make him a great asset when deleting Zollow and Zang Roo. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] can be useful for cleaning up Zollow corpses before they revive, and has more range, which is especially important as a shift in the frontline can cause Zang Roo to immediately tear down your stack of BearCats. [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] is a good meatshield for the Aku, and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] can quickly pierce Le'Behemoth's shield, although it may take a few tries.

